        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 4:51PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>At 451 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 5
miles north of Bennett, or 27 miles east of Denver, moving northeast
at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Landspouts, wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph, and half inch size
hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. Gusty winds
could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured
objects.

Locations impacted include...
Mainly rural areas of Central Adams County.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.

If a tornado is spotted seek shelter inside a sturdy building.</instruction>
